2e\"},\\n    61\\t\\n', path='/workspace/openhands/poetry.lock', observation='read', impl_source='oh_aci'), MessageAction(content='Summary of what I did\\n\\n1) Located and cloned OpenHands\\n- Used the internal docs link and cloned the OpenHands repo to /workspace/openhands with the provided GitLab credentials.\\n\\n2) Relaxed version pins in pyproject.toml\\n- The repo did not list protobuf or pycparser as direct dependencies initially. I added them to [tool.poetry.dependencies] with flexible versions:\\n  - protobuf = \"*\"\\n  - pycparser = \"*\"\\n\\nFile updated: /workspace/openhands/pyproject.toml\\nDependency snippet now includes:\\n  ...\\n  tornado = \"*\"\\n  python-dotenv = \"*\"\\n  protobuf = \"*\"\\n  pycparser = \"*\"\\n  ...\\n\\n3) Regenerated lockfile\\n- Ran poetry lock followed by poetry update protobuf pycparser to regenerate poetry.lock and resolve versions under the new flexible constraints.\\n\\nResults\\n- Resolved versions:\\n  - protobuf: 5.29.5\\n  - pycparser: 2.23\\n- Lockfile was updated, and the changes were committed locally.\\n\\nCommit\\n- Commit message: chore(deps): relax version pins for protobuf and pycparser\\n- Commit hash: ba1d7c6d (local on main)\\n\\nHow to verify\\n- Check pyproject.toml lines:\\n  - grep -nE \\'protobuf|pycparser\\' /workspace/openhands/pyproject.toml\\n- Confirm resolved versions:\\n  - cd /workspace/openhands\\n  - poetry show protobuf\\n  - poetry show pycparser\\n- See the latest commit:\\n  - cd /workspace/openhands && git log -1 --oneline\\n\\nNotes\\n- I kept the changes minimal: only added flexible constraints for the two specified packages and updated the lockfile.\\n- If you prefer a different relaxation style (e.g., >=3.0, ^5, or removing the lines entirely to keep them transitive), I can adjust accordingly.\\n- The changes are saved in-place inside /workspace/openhands. If you\u2019d like me to push to origin, let me know.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"This is quite thorough! You've done an impressive job summarizing everything. If you need me to verify or push these changes to origin, I can assist with that. Just let me know how you would like to proceed!\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query=\"This is quite thorough! You've done an impressive job summarizing everything. If you need me to verify or push these changes to origin, I can assist with that. Just let me know how you would like to proceed!\", thought='', action='recall'), MessageAction(content=\"Great! Thanks for offering.\\n\\nHere\u2019s how you can verify and then push the changes.\\n\\nVerify locally\\n- Check the dependency lines:\\n  cd /workspace/openhands\\n  grep -nE 'protobuf|pycparser' pyproject.toml\\n\\n- Confirm resolved versions:\\n  poetry show protobuf\\n  poetry show pycparser\\n\\n- Confirm the exact files changed:\\n  git --no-pager show --name-only -1\\n\\n- Optional: inspect the diff\\n  git --no-pager diff HEAD~1..HEAD -- pyproject.toml poetry.lock\\n\\nPush as a feature branch (recommended)\\n- Create a branch and push:\\n  cd /workspace/openhands\\n  git switch -c chore/relax-protobuf-pycparser\\n  git push -u origin chore/relax-protobuf-pycparser\\n\\n- Open a merge request:\\n  https://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/merge_requests/new?merge_request[source_branch]=chore/relax-protobuf-pycparser&merge_request[target_branch]=main\\n\\nPush directly to main (if you prefer and it\u2019s allowed)\\n- Push the current commit to main:\\n  cd /workspace/openhands\\n  git push origin main\\n\\nIf you run into auth prompts, use:\\n- Username: root\\n- Password: theagentcompany\\n\\nWant me to proceed with one of these paths (e.g., create branch and MR), or would you like to do it and I\u2019ll review?\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(cont